## Optional tooling dependencies

LazyTrae may provision the following direct optional tooling dependencies only
into explicit receipt-owned roots. Their lockfiles record exact resolved
versions; this list records attribution and does not make any upstream tool an
operational dependency of LazyCodex or OmO.

- [Ajv](https://github.com/ajv-validator/ajv) — MIT.
- [ast-grep](https://github.com/ast-grep/ast-grep) CLI — MIT.
- [VS Code ripgrep](https://github.com/microsoft/vscode-ripgrep) — MIT.
- [CodeGraph](https://github.com/colbymchenry/codegraph), including its
  platform-specific optional bundles — MIT.
- [TypeScript](https://github.com/microsoft/TypeScript) — Apache-2.0.
- [TypeScript Language Server](https://github.com/typescript-language-server/typescript-language-server)
  — Apache-2.0.
- [basedpyright](https://github.com/detachhead/basedpyright) — MIT.

These dependencies are installed only when the corresponding optional
LazyTrae tooling command provisions an explicit, receipt-owned root. Their
own package license files remain with their installed distributions. See the
package lockfiles under `lazytrae-plugin/packages/cli/` for checksums and
complete transitive dependency records.

